{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "RUP vs UML \"Rational Unified Process vs Unified Modelling Language\"", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear and use whenever you talk about RUP and UML.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Talk about particular topics related to software programming.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "software development", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a process to program a computer in order to get a software product", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We decided to acquire a framework for software development with adaptable methodologies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "graphical modeling", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way of encoding a graph based representation over a multi-dimensional space, expressing a conditional dependence to visualize the domain model", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  UML is a standardized graphical modeling language, which can be used to illustrate different issues about any project or system. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "abstract model", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a model that represents an extension of the reality", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)  ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: UML offers a general-purpose modeling language to display an abstract model of a system.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "prescriptive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "expressed as exactly as it is, that expresses literally how a process should be developed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: RUP is not a single concrete prescriptive process but an adaptable framework.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pick out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to gather, to select from a group", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  About the difference, I can tell you that RUP provides you with a variety of practices to pick out and build specific types of software to start a development process.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about UML and RUP. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify the main functionalities of each tool. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a brochure to explain how these tools work. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give examples in your explanation.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your brochure with a partner. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for more information about UML and RUP. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify the main functionalities of each tool.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a brochure to explain how these tools work.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give examples, ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my brochure with a partner. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Be Used To + Ing In Negative", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <strong>used to</strong> when you are accustomed to something or you don't find it unusual.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The expression <strong>be used to</strong> is sometimes followed by the gerund \u2013 the <strong>ing</strong> form of a verb.</br></br>  With <b>be used to</b> in negative you usually talk about something that is not familiar to us or easy for us. </br></br>  For negative sentences use this structure:</br></br>  <div align=\"center\">Subject + verb <strong>be</strong> (am, is, are) + <strong>not</strong> + <strong>used to</strong> + <strong>verb</strong> + <strong>ing</strong> + complement.</div></br>  Example:</br></br>  <i>I'm <strong>not used to programming</strong> in both, RUP and UML. </br>He <strong>isn't used to modeling</strong> with UML tools.</br> I <strong>am not used to working</strong> with adaptable software.</i></br></br>  Be used to can be used with contractions: </br></br>  <i>He <strong>is not used</strong> to designing systems through UML.</i> </br><i>He <strong>isn't used</strong> to designing systems through UML.</i></br></br>  Note: Remember that as they are expressions, be used to and get used to, will always be followed by a verb with ing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Isn't your staff used to programming using those tools? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Well, I'm not used to coding either in RUP or UML.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Your team is not used to working with those software tools yet. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The staff is not used to changing framework continuously, however they agreed to use it, once they saw the advantages.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Collective nouns vs Compound nouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<b>Collective nouns</b> are the ones which name a group of individuals or a number of animals, places, things, objects, concepts and others, while the <b>compound nouns</b> are the result of combining two words.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Collective nouns</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>compound nouns</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name a group\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Merge two or three words \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Some common collective nouns that are considered as a singular when they represent an entity:  </br> <ul><li>audience </li> <li>team</li> <li>jury</li> <li>company</li> <li>committee</li> <li>crowd</li> <li>class</li> <li>group </li> <li>team</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Observe some common compound nouns and the kind of part that compound those: </br> <ul><li>software (adjective \u2013 noun)</li> <li>input (adverb - verb)</li> <li>spreadsheet (verb-noun)</li> <li>blackboard  (adjective \u2013 noun)</li> <li>framework   (noun- verb)</li> <li>coding machine (gerund- noun)</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If you think of such noun as a group that is acting individually you can use a plural verb: </br> <ul><li>The staff are working in different departments. </li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You can write compound nouns in different ways: </br> <ul><li>separate words (post office)</li> <li>words linked by a hyphen (check-in)</li> <li>one word (notebook)</li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "How is your company working now? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The staff is not used to changing framework continuously.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Choose the way of elaborating their own software. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It seems your team is not used to working with those software tools yet. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "UML offers a general-purpose modeling.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "RUP vs UML", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "UML is the unified modeling language to structure and visualize the design of a software system while RUP is an adaptable process framework to develop software. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <strong>UML</strong> has its roots in the object-oriented methods, it appeared as a standardized specification language for object modeling. Since then, it has been considered a general-purpose modeling language which contains many artifacts and language constructs as graphical notation.</br> The <strong>URP</strong> is a development process framework that does not imply a prescriptive but an adaptable process which means an advantage for companies that have the possibility to select the appropriate elements of the process to their needs. ", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can compare RUP and UML. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about the differences of both, RUP and UML. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can define both, RUP and UML at a general concepts.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What are